content:
An expired membership of Northgate Memberships is renewed back to active by the primary member paying one renewal fee, and the new membership year is dated by the late renewal rule: it starts the day after the lapsed expiry date when the anniversary is kept, and on the payment date when it is not.

When an expired membership is renewed, the renewal fee of a lapsed membership takes the place of the plain annual fee; an on-time renewal, a new membership, and a conversion or downgrade taken at an on-time renewal are still charged the annual fee of the tier the membership year is held at.

## What the renewal payment does

The payment of the renewal of an expired membership is the primary member's own action. One payment:

- charges the renewal fee to the payment method the member names;
- records it on the membership ledger as a renewal fee for the new membership year;
- returns the membership to active status at the stated tier, with the stated first day and expiry date of the new membership year, keeping the same membership number.

Afterwards the member's cards admit them again and the membership shows the new year's dates and tier.

## Invocation

The tool is `pay_lapsed_membership_renewal_7a245505`. It belongs to the member: member services unlocks it and hands it over, and the customer themselves runs it to pay the renewal of their own expired membership.

## Parameters

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `membership_id` | the membership reference number of the expired membership being renewed, as returned by the membership lookup and read out to the member | identifier |
| `renewal_tier` | the official tier the new membership year is held at | one of the six tier names below, exactly |
| `new_term_start_date` | the first day of the new membership year | calendar date YYYY-MM-DD, local club date, no time part, never empty |
| `new_expiry_date` | the last day of the new membership year | calendar date YYYY-MM-DD, local club date, no time part, never empty |
| `renewal_fee` | the renewal fee charged | USD with 2 decimal places, always positive; stored rounded half up to 2 decimal places as passed, with no tax added |
| `tender` | how the member pays | one of the tender codes below |

`renewal_tier` takes exactly one of:
  - Northgate Student Club Membership — the discounted student tier, kept only while the student verification is valid;
  - Northgate Heroes Club Membership — the discounted military and first-responder tier, kept only while the service verification is valid;
  - Northgate Club Membership — the standard consumer tier, also the tier a lapsed Student Club or Heroes Club renewal converts to;
  - Northgate Business Membership — the standard business tier held in a licensed business name;
  - Northgate Club Plus Membership — the consumer Plus tier that earns Annual Reward;
  - Northgate Business Plus Membership — the business Plus tier that earns Annual Reward.

`tender` takes exactly one of:
  - `cash_or_debit` — paid from a debit card or cash at a counter;
  - `northgate_visa` — charged to the member's Northgate Rewards Visa card;
  - `northgate_store_card` — charged to the member's Northgate Store Card;
  - `other_credit_card` — charged to any other credit card the member names;
  - `shop_card` — paid from a Northgate Shop Card balance;
  - `reward_certificate` — paid with an Annual Reward certificate;
  - `not_applicable` — never used for a payment, only for entries that carry no payment.

## Return

A text receipt reading "Renewal paid", followed by the renewal entry reference on the membership ledger, the membership reference, the amount charged in USD with 2 decimals, the tender, the tier now held, the new membership year's first day and expiry date (YYYY-MM-DD), and the status "active". A receipt starting "Renewal paid" means the charge and the reactivation are both recorded.

## Points of reference

- *Which memberships does this concern?* A membership whose status is expired. An active membership renewed on or before its expiry date is an on-time renewal and is charged the annual fee of the tier its year is held at.
- *What does the member see afterwards?* The membership active again under the same number, with the new year's tier and dates, and a renewal fee entry for that year on the ledger.
